    "source": "Happy Birthday: the melody of happy-birthday.json (version 6), note for note, down a whole step to F, sung twice with a bar's rest between (Hillel, 2026-11-22: \"change Happy Birthday to just Happy Birthday\"); its sources are in that template. Kept for a later template of its own, For He's a Jolly Good Fellow (versions 1 to 3 sang it after Happy Birthday): \"For He's a Jolly Good Fellow!\", No. 61 in Peter W. Dykema, Will Earhart, Osbourne McConathy and Hollis Dann, eds., Twice 55 Community Songs, No. 1: The Brown Book (Boston: C. C. Birchard, copyright 1919), archive.org/details/twice55community01dyke (leaf n38), the verse ending \"which nobody can deny!\", G major 6/8, its melody (the top of the printed chords) note for note, moved to A-flat, down a major sixth from the F of version 2, 11 semitones below the print's G, so its first note is Happy Birthday's first note (Hillel, 2026-11-22: \"can Jolly Good Fellow start at the same note?\"), each eighth half a beat of 3/4; \"you're\" for the print's \"he's\"; no fermatas; the last \"ny!\" held to the bar's end; checked against Louis C. Elson, Folk Songs of Many Nations (Cincinnati: John Church, 1905), p. 52, archive.org/details/bub_gb_FCvaAAAAMAAJ (leaf n57), the same tune in G 6/8, whose verse ends \"So say we all of us\" and whose pickups are two sixteenths"
